      <h2 class="vf-section-header__heading" id="about-heading">About the BioinfoTraining Community</h2>
    </div>
    <p>The BioinfoTraining Community is a collaborative platform supported by EMBL-EBI Training and partner organisations. It enables scientific communities to share and develop training resources, improve accessibility across languages and regions, and exchange knowledge and expertise.</p>
    <p>The platform encourages community contributions through the collaborative development, translation and adaptation of training materials, helping make bioinformatics education more accessible to learners worldwide.</p>
    <p>Each community has its own dedicated space to share training resources, highlight activities and foster collaboration around specific scientific topics.</p>
    <p>Our first community, <a class="vf-link" href="/spaces/alphafold/">AlphaFold and Structural Biology</a>, brings together educators, researchers and learners interested in protein structure prediction and structural bioinformatics. Its development has benefited from the support and expertise of the Protein Data Bank in Europe (PDBe) and the AlphaFold Protein Structure Database (AlphaFold DB). A key activity of this community is the translation and adaptation of training tutorials into different languages, led by members of the AlphaFold Education Community in coordination with the EMBL-EBI Training and Web Development teams. These collaborative efforts aim to make training resources more accessible to learners across different languages and regions.</p>
    <p>As the platform evolves, we aim to welcome additional scientific communities, supporting a growing network of shared knowledge, resources and expertise.</p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="soft-launch-heading" class="vf-u-margin__top--800">
    <div class="vf-section-header">
      <h2 class="vf-section-header__heading" id="soft-launch-heading">Soft launch – Help us shape the Community Space</h2>
    </div>
    <p>The BioinfoTraining Community is currently in its soft launch phase, ahead of a wider public release. During this initial stage, we are testing the platform, reviewing its content and functionality, and gathering feedback to guide further improvements.</p>
    <p>We invite you to explore the platform and share your observations, suggestions and ideas. Your feedback will help us identify areas for improvement and shape the next stages of development.</p>
    <p>Thank you for helping us build a community space that meets the needs of its users!</p>
